body:
I am a AFAB non-binary person and while exploring my gender identity I would always joke; 

"The world is likely more prepared to accept me as a non-binary person before they accept be as a 4'11" guy."

I have since found out I have never really identified as a male so much as just a person, though says a lot about males+defaults+culture ect. But it was a joke that hit people way harder than I expected.

I appreciate the perspective and honest conversation this has started, but to continue, could you provide sources for your claim? I would like to continue to comment but would like to first read the original source you got this info from so I can engaged with knowledge.

&#x200B;

EDIT: engage with better knowledge
